\begin{itemize}
\item Convex functions lie below their tangent lines
\item Expectation is a weighted average
\item Applying a convex function after averaging is less than averaging after applying the function
\item Geometrically, the function's curve is 'bent upwards'
\end{itemize}

\begin{itemize}
\item Martingales: sequences with 'fair game' property
\item Applying convex functions to martingales yields submartingales
\item Jensen's Inequality applied to conditional expectations
\item Fundamental in stochastic process theory and finance
\end{itemize}

\begin{itemize}
\item Extensions to infinite-dimensional spaces
\item Applications in modern machine learning frameworks
\item Deeper exploration in stochastic analysis and financial mathematics
\item Development of new inequalities inspired by Jensen's framework
\end{itemize}

\begin{itemize}
\item Hardy, Littlewood, Pólya (1934) - Inequalities
\item Rockafellar (1970) - Convex Analysis
\item Durrett (2019) - Probability: Theory and Examples
\item Shreve (2004) - Stochastic Calculus for Finance
\end{itemize}
